  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigating Conflict in Abyei through Water Interventions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is based on a multi-sectoral and community-based approach that focuses on addressing identified humanitarian and early recovery needs of the most vulnerable and marginalized communities, while strengthening community stabilization, security and resilience to support durable solutions for displaced populations such as IDPs and returnees in Sudan. The multi-sectorial interventions undertaken by the project will include a number of sub-components: (1) gathering information and data through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) for IOM, the Government of Sudan, and partners to use as an evidence base for planning and implementing interventions; (2) increasing access to clean and safe water for those affected by conflict-related displacement, natural disasters, climate shocks and disease outbreaks through the repair of existing water points; (3) delivering a minimum Basic Package of Primary Health care Services (BPPHS) as well as building the capacity of local service providers, with COVID-19 prevention and response plans for conflict effected communities; and (4) delivering improved livelihood opportunities with focus on strengthening the empowerment of youth and women for supporting long-term economic development in conflict and displacement effected areas.</narrative>
  </description>
